Lunaris (Xiaomi) Dolby
==============


Getting Started
---------------

### Codecs (AC3, Spatial)
For Dolby media codecs to work, add this line in your media codecs config (should be in vendor partition) and make sure your device supports c2 codecs. 

```bash
<Include href="media_codecs_dolby_audio.xml" />
```
### Effects 

To build, add the Dolby effects in your device's audio effects config, then inherit the Dolby config by adding this in your device's makefile:

```makefile
$(call inherit-product, hardware/dolby/dolby.mk)
```
> You may want to use `inherit-product-if-exists`, otherwise building will terminate if `hardware/dolby/dolby.mk` does not exist.


Now, moving HIDL definitions in manifest to device trees is completely absurd, so stop overriding manifests in your device trees.
An example for such would be changing these in BoardConfig.mk of your device tree:

```makefile
DEVICE_FRAMEWORK_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE :=
```
To:

```makefile
DEVICE_FRAMEWORK_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE +=
```

Be sure to include the VINTF makefile **after** your BoardConfig.mk VINTF declarations.
```makefile
include hardware/dolby/configs/vintf/config.mk
```
> Use `-include` instead to prevent failure if hardware/dolby isn't present.

Build Flags
------------

```
TARGET_BUILD_DOLBY_EFFECTS :=
TARGET_BUILD_DOLBY_CODECS :=
```

Both of these are set to true by default by dolby.mk if not overridden. If you only want to build the effects, set `TARGET_BUILD_DOLBY_CODECS := false` in your device tree and vice versa.
